# MT7925FW (zenbook-ledger Z5, ZENBOOKMT7925; the FWPIN shape of rmbp-ledger B455) — SHA-256 pins for the MediaTek MT7925
# Wi-Fi 7 firmware pair (drivers/mt7925.rs). NO FIRMWARE BYTES live in this tree (R52, CLEAN_ROOM_POLICY §4). Each row is a
# fact ABOUT a file the operator fetches from linux-firmware: `<role> <64 lowercase hex>`, roles patch / ram. The probe hashes
# the pair on the ESP at FW/MT7925/ (arroyo's MT7925-FW line, `fw_stage_pinned`, from UNAOS_MT7925_FW_PATH) and reads
# patch_sha= / ram_sha= ok|mismatch|unpinned; nothing is uploaded at S1.
# A newer linux-firmware drop changes both digests: the MT7925-FW build line prints the new rows (`pin-row: <role> <hex>`).
# Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
# 2026-10-28 (the bench): re-pinned to the bench's drop, Fedora linux-firmware-20261019-1.fc44 (/lib/firmware/mediatek/mt7925, the
# .xz pair decompressed into ~/unaos-bench/firmware/mediatek-mt7925); the previous rows were another drop's (the build line read MISMATCH).

